Very good points.

To be clear, however, the discussion over property rights in land is
not whether to respect property rights as such (which I feel is a
nonsensical question, if property is used with a sensible definition),
but when to respect a claim to a property right. I need not treat
something as someone else's property simply because they claim it is
their property. Under what conditions does it makes sense for me to do
so? Under what conditions should I lend my support/moral sanction to
their property claim?

